    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Developer Overview – FOI Audit Retention\n\n**Purpose:** keeps `foi-process-audit` and `foi-execution-errors` from growing without limit (the n8n Data Tables share an instance-wide size cap).\n\n**Trigger:** every Sunday 2 AM. Created INACTIVE: activate only after the FOI records owners set the retention periods in `Retention Settings` (placeholders: audit 180 days, errors 365 days).\n\n**Processing:** deletes rows older than the cutoff by `createdAt`. This is safe because nothing in the event flow reads these tables any more: duplicate and ordering checks and the failed-execution lookup use the API outbox in Postgres. The event payload stays in the outbox until its own retention (N8N_OUTBOX_SCRUB_AFTER_DAYS / N8N_OUTBOX_PURGE_AFTER_DAYS).\n\n**Not purged:** `foi-payment-sla` (a late payment still needs its row).\n\n**Failures** go to FOI Error Handler (error workflow).",
        "height": 332,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "c3d4e5f6-0011-4c00-8000-000000000011",
      "name": "Developer Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -272,
        -368
      ]
    }
  ],
